axis_cusp: p=-3*a^2, c=2*a^3+h
Delta=-27*h*(4*a^3+h); Jacobian at (a,h)=(1,0) is -6
Hermite coordinates per normal polynomial: P(a), P'(a), P(-2*a)
K0=L^2*(L+3); nilradical N=L*(L+3); N^2=K0*(L+3)
alpha=2beta control: Q1=q*N, R2=q^2/3, tail_3beta=-4*q^3/81 polynomial
quartic common numerator mod K0=(q^4/243)*(5*L^2+18*L+15)
arbitrary Q2,R3 corrections are multiples of K0 in that numerator
row3 target is also a K0 multiple; row6 subtracts only a scalar
scope: this kills the displayed hidden branch, not all tropical branches
PASS-D1-DOUBLE-ROOT-NEWTON-STRUCTURE-V3
